    <string name="settings_drive_title">Google Drive</string>
    <string name="settings_drive_intro_title">You will need your own Google API key</string>
    <string name="settings_drive_intro_body">This app has no built-in Google account, and that is on purpose. Google caps unverified apps at 100 users for life, so a shared key would stop working for everyone after the hundredth person. Your own key has no cap, costs nothing, and nobody can take it away.

It takes about five minutes, once.</string>
    <string name="settings_drive_step_1">1. Open console.cloud.google.com and create a project.</string>
    <string name="settings_drive_step_2">2. Under APIs &amp; Services, enable the Google Drive API.</string>
    <string name="settings_drive_step_3">3. Configure the OAuth consent screen. Choose External, add yourself as a test user, and add the scope .../auth/drive.file</string>
    <string name="settings_drive_step_4">4. Under Credentials, create an OAuth client ID of type <b>Desktop app</b>. It must be Desktop — Android clients cannot use this sign-in.</string>
    <string name="settings_drive_step_5">5. Copy the client ID and client secret here.</string>
